*Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP)*: Objects in a program should be replaceable with instances of their subtypes without altering the correctness of that program. Observe the two classes below. The method read in FileInputStream returns the next byte of data or -1 if the end of the file is reached. The method read in EndlessFileInputStream returns the next byte of data or the first byte of the file if the end of the file is reached. LSP is violated here. Explain the issue.

